      :file
      "packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/infra/cli/commands/sol.cljs",
      :detail
      "live-pid (lines 87-94) trusts any pidfile whose pid passes `kill -0`, and stop-impl (lines 149-166) then SIGTERMs it. Reproduced live during this review: a stale `.eta-mu-sol/sol.pid` at the repo root named pid 685792, which was a live process but not sol (nothing listening on the probed port; the last real sol server in sol.log was a different pid). `sol start` refused to start ('sol is already running (pid 685792, port 8177)'), `sol status` reported 'process: running' with health unreachable, and `sol stop` sent SIGTERM to that foreign pid and reported success. After any pid recycle (reboot, long uptime), `stop` kills an arbitrary process and `start` is blocked by a phantom. The card's claim 'clears stale pidfiles' only holds when the stale pid is dead. Before SIGTERM, verify identity — e.g. /proc/<pid>/cmdline contains the resolved server path, or record the launched port in the state dir and require a matching /health — and have start treat a non-sol pid as stale.",
